      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We have $AC$ is the length of the side opposite to $\\angle A$.\n\nFrom the Pythagorean Theorem, we have $(AC)^2 + (AB)^2 = (BC)^2$.\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get $(AC)^2 + (16)^2 = (24)^2$.\n\nSimplifying, we have $(AC)^2 = (24)^2 - (16)^2$.\n\nFactoring, we get $(AC)^2 = (24+16)(24-16)$.\n\nSimplifying, we have $(AC)^2 = 40\\times 8$.\n\nTaking the square root of both sides, we get $(AC) = 8\\sqrt{5}$.\n\nThus, $\\sin A = \\frac{AC}{BC} = \\frac{8\\sqrt{5}}{24} = \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}}$.The answer is: \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}",
